course: dictionary
lesson: 2459
title: Words from French in ballet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come into English from other languages and keep their original shape. Danseur is a French word, and English uses it for a male ballet dancer. «The premier danseur leaped high across the stage.» The word premier tells you he is the leading dancer, and leaping high tells you he is dancing.
explain: Ballet has many French words, such as plié, pirouette and pas de deux. Use the context to work out their meaning. A danseur partners the ballerina, lifting and supporting her and dancing solos with big jumps.
explain: French job words often change their ending to show whether a man or a woman does the job. «Job words change in patterns: boulanger to boulangère, chanteur to chanteuse, acteur to actrice; so danseur gives danseuse, fermier gives fermière and directeur gives directrice.» Spotting the pattern helps you guess new job words.
fact: Danseur means male ballet dancer, and it comes from French.
fact: In French, «danseur» simply means «dancer», a man who dances.
fact: «Premier danseur» means a leading male dancer in a ballet company.
fact: «Danseur noble» means a dancer of princely, classical roles.
fact: Female forms follow patterns: «danseur» gives «danseuse», «fermier» gives «fermière», «directeur» gives «directrice».
exercise: «The premier danseur leaped high across the stage.» What is a danseur? | A stage light | A French town | *A male ballet dancer | A female singer
exercise: In French, what does «danseur» simply mean? | A theatre seat | *A dancer, a man who dances | A ballet shoe | A tall jump
exercise: Following the job word pattern, what is the female form of danseur? | directrice | dansant | *danseuse | danseurs
test: The word «danseur» comes from which language? | German | Italian | *French | Spanish
test: In a ballet duet, what does a danseur do for the ballerina? | Sews her costume | Plays the music | Sells the tickets | *Lifts and supports her
exam: Using the pattern «boulanger» to «boulangère», what is the female form of «directeur»? | directors | *directrice | directeur | directer
